  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="55a48873-0937-560e-bb12-c2b5fff2822e" activityNameId="5e758e21-4cac-50f9-ad4e-b7b4892e0f14" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Calcium nitrate, as N, at regional storehouse</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Calcium nitrate, as N, at regional storehouse
Refers to 1 kg N, resp. 6.45 kg calcium nitrate with a N-content of 15.5%;
CAS number: 010124-37-5; 
Formula: Ca(NO3)2(H2O)4; 
Synonyms: CaN; 
UUID: 90c2d19f-09cf-3144-b264-f40b2a91a024
The unit process inventory takes into account the use of energy resources, cited in Kongshaug (1998), needed for the production of calcium nitrate as by-product during the manufacture of NPK fertilisers. These values must be considered as uncertain, because the system boundaries were not clearly defined by Kongshaug. Infrastructure was included by means of a proxy module.
Location: According to the reference used for this inventory, the European average is derived from mean values of several fertiliser plants within Europe.
Technology: Energy inputs were derived from detailed literature studies and specifications from the manufacturer, relevant for the European production.
Time period: Year when the principal reference used for this inventory was published.
Production volume: na
Sampling: Values given in the reference originate from manufacturers and/or other data sources which in turn refer to the real situation and hence are largely secured. However, the emissions factors may be somewhat uncertain. When no information on the speciation of N - emissions was given in the reference, the most likely speciation was assessed by an expert. For particulate emissions factors into the air specified only as the total particle mass in the reference, particle size distribution was assessed based on an expert's guess. 
Extrapolations: Extrapolated from the total process and feedstock energy required for the production. No further information given on representativeness. 
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_90c2d19f-09cf-3144-b264-f40b2a91a024.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
